    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > is a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/1/c419798249c4890a933054c0a0730e7888eaec76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"93\" height=\"33\" > and the circumradius equal to 1. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > is a point inside or in its boundary let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29adc97a55365c1c6ef1ca9a295f4e7bda4fe6a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m(X)=\\min(AX,BX,CX).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" > Find all the angles of this triangle if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/0935625275487d0836901a967cc48b0c2fadd9ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\max(m(X))=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"150\" height=\"41\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Let $ABC$ is a triangle with $\\angle BAC=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ and the circumradius equal to 1. If $X$ is a point inside or in its boundary let $m(X)=\\min(AX,BX,CX).$ Find all the angles of this triangle if $\\max(m(X))=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$",
